This paper aims to establish robust and straightforward $\mathbf{L}^{\infty}$ estimates for solutions of parabolic complex Monge-Ampère and related equations. As applications, we derive multiple $L^{\infty}$ estimates for the Monge-Ampère equation by leveraging its parabolic nature and obtain the first $L^{\infty}$ bounds for solutions of the Gaussian equation. Notably, these results impose no constraints on growth at infinity for initial data or boundary functions. Furthermore, our findings offer more precise $L^{\infty}$ estimates for the classical Chen-Zhang solution of the Monge-Ampère equation. The applications demonstrate broad applicability, and the methods appear extendable to other complex Hessian equations. Specifically, for solutions to the Chen-Zhang equation satisfying appropriate initial and boundary conditions, we obtain the following $C^{0}$ estimate:
\begin{align*}
\max_{\overline{\Omega}}u(\cdot,t)\leq C\left(1+\max_{\partial\Omega}u(\cdot,\cdot)\right)\left(1+\max_{\overline{\Omega}}u_{0}\right),
\end{*}$
where $u_{0}$ denotes the initial condition, $u$ is the solution, and $C$ is a constant independent of $u$. This represents the first $C^{0}$ estimate for the Chen-Zhang solution. Additionally, for parabolic complex Monge-Ampère equations and related systems satisfying suitable initial and boundary conditions, the following $C^{0}$ estimate holds:
\begin{align*}
\max_{\overline{\Omega}}u(\cdot,t)\leq C\left(1+\max_{\partial\Omega}u(\cdot,\cdot)\right)+C\max_{\overline{\Omega}}u_{0},
\end{*}
where $u_{0}$ is the initial condition, $u$ is the solution, and $C$ is a constant independent of $u$. This paper presents the first $C^{0}$ estimate for this category of equations. The remainder of the paper is organized as follows: Section 2 reviews the Chen-Zhang solution of the parabolic complex Monge-Ampère equation; Section 3 proves the $C^{0}$ estimate for the Chen-Zhang solution; and Section 4 develops the $C^{0}$ estimate for parabolic complex Monge-Ampère

